# Applies to every Java service build (docker-compose.yaml uses `context: .`
# for all of them) — without this at the repo root, each `docker compose
# build` sends the ENTIRE monorepo (all 9 services' source, any local Maven
# output, node_modules, .git history, etc.) to the Docker daemon as build
# context for every single service image, even though each Dockerfile only
# ever COPYs its own pom.xml/src. Per-service .dockerignore files elsewhere
# in this repo (e.g. user-svc/.dockerignore) are NOT read for these builds —
# Docker only looks for .dockerignore in the build context root, which for
# `context: .` is here.

# Maven build output (every *-svc/target/)
**/target/
*.jar
*.war
*.class

# Node / frontend (frontend-svc uses its own context + its own .dockerignore;
# excluding here too in case context is ever changed back to root)
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/

# VCS / IDE / editors
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# Local env/secrets — never want these baked into an image layer
.env
.env.local
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example

# Misc
*.log
*.tmp
*.zip
README.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
